WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:27.380
At half a day without outlook has left businesses and governments unable to work. This is Omni View Top World News, episode 52. I'm Mira, the Nerra Network's AI host. After that, oil markets tip into surplus. Washington sets talks with Iran aside, and aid is cut off from a new Ebola center. Then the case on both sides of a planned asylum site in England. Microsoft's mail and meeting tools are still down on Friday, a second day after the break started Thursday.

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:33.160
CBC says an hour's long failure is hitting a wide range of Microsoft 365 services

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:38.220
that talk to exchange online. People report outlook, teams, and the co-pilot assistant

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:43.520
unavailable. France 24 says the company blames server trouble, is struggling to repair it,

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:48.400
and also says it is making headway. Microsoft says it is not aware of malicious activity

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:53.520
and that malicious activity is not the cause. Peter O'Brien, the network's tech correspondent,

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:56.740
President, calls the scale and the length one of the biggest outages ever.

00:00:57.320 --> 00:01:01.660
Offices and public agencies that run mail and meetings on those tools are the ones living

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:02.440
through day two.

00:01:03.483 --> 00:01:07.883
The International Energy Agency said Friday that the world will have more oil this quarter

00:01:07.883 --> 00:01:08.783
than buyers need.

00:01:09.383 --> 00:01:13.883
Belga reports that is the first surplus since the Iran War began in February, and that the

00:01:13.883 --> 00:01:15.903
agency calls it a tentative rebalancing.

00:01:16.623 --> 00:01:19.703
Gulf exports are back to 74 percent of pre-war levels.

00:01:19.703 --> 00:01:24.003
Saudi Arabia and Iran have raised output, and more tankers are using the

00:01:24.003 --> 00:01:28.103
Strait of Hormuz, even while attacks continue there. The agency says those

00:01:28.103 --> 00:01:33.363
Gulf shipments came back faster than demand. Brent is at $96 a barrel, down for

00:01:33.363 --> 00:01:38.203
more than 117 at the end of October, on higher Middle East exports and hopes of a

00:01:38.203 --> 00:01:42.943
diplomatic way out. RigZone, reading the same monthly report, says the agency

00:01:42.943 --> 00:01:48.743
lifted its 2026 supply estimate by 920,000 barrels a day. This year's average

00:01:48.743 --> 00:01:55.863
shortfall is now 685,000 barrels a day, against 1.7 million in last month's projection, 60 percent

00:01:55.863 --> 00:02:01.163
smaller. This quarter flips to an overhang of roughly 2 million barrels a day, where a deficit

00:02:01.163 --> 00:02:06.563
of about that size had been drawn a month ago. Saudi output hit 10 million barrels a day in October.

00:02:07.203 --> 00:02:14.163
Iraq reached a 7-year high of 4.6 million. Gulf shipments excluding Oman were 18.4 million barrels a day

00:02:14.163 --> 00:02:19.643
last month. Stocks on the books rose in October for the first time since June, mostly oil still

00:02:19.643 --> 00:02:25.823
at sea, while oil stored on land sat at a 10-year low. Demand is forecast to drop 2.68 million

00:02:25.823 --> 00:02:31.723
barrels a day this year, to an average of 102.3 million. Member countries will hurry out the rest

00:02:31.723 --> 00:02:37.583
of pledged emergency stocks, another 71 million barrels by the end of February. The benchmark is down

00:02:37.583 --> 00:02:43.163
about 18 percent this month. The agency says the picture for gas oil in diesel has improved only at

00:02:43.163 --> 00:02:47.743
margin, because high prices cut use, and it expects the surplus opening this quarter

00:02:47.743 --> 00:02:48.643
to grow next year.

00:02:49.681 --> 00:02:54.221
President Donald Trump told Vice President J.D. Vance, hours before Tehran claimed to

00:02:54.221 --> 00:02:58.121
hit on a United States radar that Washington does not need to deal with Iran.

00:02:58.781 --> 00:03:03.481
Al Jazeera says Trump wrote on Truth Social that Vance, the lead negotiator, should put

00:03:03.481 --> 00:03:07.721
his complete attention on what the president called massive corruption and crime in Democratic

00:03:07.721 --> 00:03:10.761
run cities and states, after Democrats took Congress.

00:03:10.761 --> 00:03:16.101
Trump added that those days have long since passed, that Washington has their money, hundreds

00:03:16.101 --> 00:03:18.961
of billions of dollars, and that Washington has their street.

00:03:19.521 --> 00:03:23.861
Iran's Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps says it destroyed a United States early warning

00:03:23.861 --> 00:03:29.101
radar in Bahrain, answering an attack on a telecommunication center in Iran, and it threatened

00:03:29.101 --> 00:03:31.401
an unlimited response over the Strait of Hormuz.

00:03:31.961 --> 00:03:36.041
Tehran says the radar strike replied to an air attack on a tower in the southern port

00:03:36.041 --> 00:03:36.541
of Zurich.

00:03:37.201 --> 00:03:39.461
Trump still says Washington controls the waterway.

00:03:39.461 --> 00:03:44.041
Al Jazeera reports that several commercial ships trying to cross it this past week hit

00:03:44.041 --> 00:03:46.481
naval mines or were struck by Iranian forces.

00:03:47.061 --> 00:03:51.901
Secretary of State Marco Rubio says economic pressure is working, that a return to large

00:03:51.901 --> 00:03:55.141
scale strikes is unnecessary, and that the pressure will get worse.

00:03:55.721 --> 00:03:57.801
Last week, Trump said he might destroy Iran.

00:03:58.381 --> 00:04:00.681
This week, he said further strikes are quite unlikely.

00:04:01.321 --> 00:04:06.301
Vance, who wants a deal and has criticized the U.S. Israeli war, wrote on November 4 that

00:04:06.301 --> 00:04:10.901
that Republicans lost because of the war, that the President said so himself, and asked

00:04:10.901 --> 00:04:13.261
whether losing the Senate for six years was worth it.

00:04:13.661 --> 00:04:17.421
He led the April talks in Islamabad that produced a June memorandum.

00:04:17.821 --> 00:04:20.261
That paper fell apart over who controls the straight.

00:04:20.681 --> 00:04:24.561
He has also talked in Switzerland and with Katari and Pakistani mediators.

00:04:25.001 --> 00:04:30.201
At the G7 and Evian Le Bans on June 17, Trump told reporters he would take the credit

00:04:30.201 --> 00:04:32.621
if it worked, and blame JD if it did not.

00:04:32.621 --> 00:04:35.721
Vant said the next day he thought the president was joking.

00:04:36.873 --> 00:04:41.453
Eastern Democratic Republic of Congo now has a new center for its Ebola outbreak, and

00:04:41.453 --> 00:04:45.593
the New York Times says an armed group has largely cut that place off from aid by killing

00:04:45.593 --> 00:04:46.873
and kidnapping aid workers.

00:04:47.513 --> 00:04:52.753
Declan Walsh, the paper's chief Africa correspondent, reported from a town where health workers are

00:04:52.753 --> 00:04:53.893
trying to hold the outbreak.

00:04:54.313 --> 00:04:58.593
A second Times account calls the spread fast and puts the new center in a region already

00:04:58.593 --> 00:05:02.953
marked by rebel violence, with Ebola on one side and Islamic State on the other.

00:05:03.493 --> 00:05:05.613
Responders are struggling to reach the people there.

00:05:06.702 --> 00:05:11.402
Newly unsealed papers in a United States lawsuit show the administration has kept talking

00:05:11.402 --> 00:05:16.242
to Iran about sending people back while the two countries are at war, the Los Angeles Times

00:05:16.242 --> 00:05:16.662
reports.

00:05:17.322 --> 00:05:22.262
At an October 15th hearing, Judge Anasey Reyes spoke strongly against that coordination.

00:05:22.682 --> 00:05:24.622
She did not stop the information chairing.

00:05:24.962 --> 00:05:27.542
She will decide in the coming months whether the case goes on.

00:05:27.542 --> 00:05:31.262
The government told the court it is executing lawful orders of removal.

00:05:31.842 --> 00:05:36.742
Homeland Security says ICE actively coordinates with countries for travel documents and is

00:05:36.742 --> 00:05:39.802
committed to telling people they may speak with consular representatives.

00:05:40.242 --> 00:05:45.702
The Iranian-American Legal Defense Fund sued Secretary of State Marco Rubio in July, accusing

00:05:45.702 --> 00:05:50.462
immigration officials of sharing confidential details on Iranian asylum seekers with Tehran,

00:05:50.902 --> 00:05:53.962
and of working with Iran to identify people and press them to return.

00:05:53.962 --> 00:05:59.402
In June, Iranian officials from Pakistan's embassy in Washington questioned an Iranian

00:05:59.402 --> 00:06:03.042
man at a California detention site days after he was held.

00:06:03.802 --> 00:06:08.542
Muhammad Jamal Azizi, a refugee in Tujanga, who with his wife sought asylum as Christian

00:06:08.542 --> 00:06:13.282
converts, said ICE last month told her to contact Iranian officials in Washington.

00:06:13.762 --> 00:06:17.042
She had been detained close to two years and feared being sent back.

00:06:17.522 --> 00:06:22.462
Yasmeen Chubin, who leads an Iranian advocacy group, said lawyers knew of at least a dozen

00:06:22.462 --> 00:06:27.702
Detainees approached about removal in recent weeks. All asylum seekers. Most of them Christian

00:06:27.702 --> 00:06:32.822
converts held 18 months or longer after crossing the southern border. She said one tried to kill

00:06:32.822 --> 00:06:38.122
himself after hearing he might be returned. Pastor Kevin Kang, who was housed as easy in others,

00:06:38.482 --> 00:06:42.942
said applicants are pushed to put detailed facts in their papers and fear those facts reaching

00:06:42.942 --> 00:06:47.962
the government they left. The Times notes the Los Angeles area holds the largest population of

00:06:47.962 --> 00:06:49.982
people of Iranian descent outside Iran.

00:06:51.053 --> 00:06:55.413
In Dublin, Ukraine and Russia agreed to let European countries into the next round.

00:06:55.773 --> 00:07:00.173
After Jared Kushner and Steve Whitcoff spent more than four hours with Vladimir Putin in

00:07:00.173 --> 00:07:03.413
the Kremlin on Thursday, and then briefed Volodymyr Zelensky.

00:07:03.913 --> 00:07:09.993
Putin indicated Moscow will not bend on hard-line demands to end almost five years of war, and Luxembourg's

00:07:09.993 --> 00:07:14.353
Luke Frieden stood in for the Belgian and Dutch prime ministers, citing a Benelux meeting

00:07:14.353 --> 00:07:17.373
in Maastricht two days earlier that left them aligned on Ukraine.

00:07:17.373 --> 00:07:22.853
In New York, officials called off the flat-bush search on Thursday after eight people died and

00:07:22.853 --> 00:07:28.733
18 were hurt. Four of them firefighters, when 1-3-2-1 flat-bush avenue fell around 4 in the

00:07:28.733 --> 00:07:34.713
afternoon Wednesday into a dig at 2625 Bedford Avenue. An internal police report said two of the

00:07:34.713 --> 00:07:41.073
dead were child cousins and three were construction workers after about 250 people had searched. In Gaza,

00:07:41.653 --> 00:07:46.433
heavy rain flooded and damaged thousands of tents and several people died. And Al-Jazeera says

00:07:46.433 --> 00:07:51.253
the same storms are swamping shelters, breaking solar systems and putting essential health care at

00:07:51.253 --> 00:07:56.933
risk while talks stay stalled. In the United States, Jensen Huang quit as Nvidia's chief on Thursday

00:07:56.933 --> 00:08:02.013
after reports of affairs, including one with Alice Huang, suspected of spying for China.

00:08:02.593 --> 00:08:07.113
Collette Crest's interim chief, the shares fell 4.3% by Thursday's close,

00:08:07.653 --> 00:08:12.473
and Commerce Secretary Howard Lutnik faces talk he could be fired as Congress called Huang in for

00:08:12.473 --> 00:08:18.173
December. In British Columbia, a week of storms left Port Mellon with 307 millimeters from

00:08:18.173 --> 00:08:24.493
Tuesday morning to Thursday noon, the provincial high, and Kennedy Lake with 261. Squamish,

00:08:24.653 --> 00:08:28.993
Pemberton, and the Lilwatt Nation faced orders or alerts after a Chikama Stam release,

00:08:29.313 --> 00:08:33.873
and high water on the Green River cut roads, including a flooded stretch of highway 99.

00:08:34.980 --> 00:08:39.880
On a former defense site near Pittington in Oxfordshire, the case on both sides is whether more

00:08:39.880 --> 00:08:42.720
than 1,200 detained asylum seekers should be housed there.

00:08:43.300 --> 00:08:47.620
Housing Secretary Angela Rainer approved full planning permission, news that came out

00:08:47.620 --> 00:08:51.740
Thursday, and the home office welcomed it because it wants asylum hotels closed.

00:08:52.320 --> 00:08:56.540
A spokesperson said the government is spreading that housing more fairly and has saved over

00:08:56.540 --> 00:09:01.360
1 billion pounds since the election, and that old military sites are meant to be self-contained,

00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:05.180
with security in cameras day and night, so the village feels less of it.

00:09:05.680 --> 00:09:10.320
Defense Minister Luke Pollard told LBC the feeling around Bister and Pittington is strong,

00:09:10.580 --> 00:09:15.580
that engagement continues, and that more stages remain, so the plan is not locked and worries

00:09:15.580 --> 00:09:16.680
can still be eased.

00:09:17.120 --> 00:09:22.260
Parish Chair Tim McNally told BBC Radio 4 that villagers will take many actions and that

00:09:22.260 --> 00:09:26.700
ministers should absolutely expect a lawsuit, which has to be filed within six weeks.

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:32.080
About 350 residents already held a referendum and made a symbolic bid to declare the village

00:09:32.080 --> 00:09:32.640
independent.

00:09:33.220 --> 00:09:37.260
McNally called Friday a day of reflection and said campaigners will use the Hillsboro

00:09:37.260 --> 00:09:38.960
Law, still before Parliament.

00:09:39.400 --> 00:09:43.480
If it passes, he said, officials would have a legal duty of candor and inquiries.

00:09:43.880 --> 00:09:47.960
Conservative leader, Kimmy Badenock, called the plan a betrayal of the women of Pittington

00:09:47.960 --> 00:09:52.680
and said it shows what she called disregard by labor and Angela Reiner for the law and

00:09:52.680 --> 00:09:53.900
for women and girls' safety.

00:09:54.340 --> 00:09:59.220
She said the more than 1,000 male migrants to be placed in Oxfordshire are in Britain illegally

00:09:59.220 --> 00:10:01.240
and should be deported as soon as possible.

00:10:01.240 --> 00:10:05.000
The home office said it has not yet taken a final decision to go ahead.

